@overheard bunkpairs
// Writer-commons, overheard batch 2. Bunkmates (pair:bunk) at the junior wing's doors, washrooms and lockers.

== overheard
? pair:bunk time:morning
A: Have you seen my other boot?
B: Lost property.
A: It's been gone ten minutes.
B: They're very efficient.   #funny

? pair:bunk time:night
A: Are you writing home?
B: Trying. I've got "Dear Mum".
A: Good start.
B: It's the middle that's hard.   #warm

? pair:bunk time:evening
A: Whose turn is it for the laundry?
B: Yours.
A: It's always mine.
B: Then you're very good at it.   #funny

? pair:bunk deck:4
A: Someone ate my biscuits.
B: Not me.
A: You've got crumbs on your chin.
B: Those are old crumbs.   #funny

? pair:bunk time:night
A: The star map's fallen down again.
B: I'll tape it tomorrow.
A: Tonight. I like falling asleep under it.

? pair:bunk time:morning
A: Your alarm went off at five.
B: That's the galley lot. Not me.
A: Then whose alarm sings?
B: That's not an alarm. That's Madsen.   #funny

? pair:bunk
A: Do you ever miss having your own room?
B: Sometimes. Then someone snores and I don't.
A: You snore too.
B: Lies.   #funny

? pair:bunk time:evening
A: Coming to the common room?
B: In a bit. Saving my seat?
A: Always.   #warm
